# Compiled programs and test binaries (e.g. from `go build` or `go test -c`)
*.exe
*.test
/bin/

# Reports written by the test commands in README.md and by CI:
# coverage (coverage.out, coverage.html), the JUnit XML report, mutation results.
/reports/
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.coverprofile

# rapid (property-based tests) saves each failing case here so the next run replays it
# first. Useful on your machine while you fix the bug, not something to commit.
testdata/rapid/

# Note: Go keeps its build and test caches outside the project
# (see `go env GOCACHE`), so there is no cache folder to ignore here.
# The fuzzer's own working corpus lives there too; only inputs that made a fuzz test
# FAIL are written to testdata/fuzz/ – keep those, they become regression tests.
